{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340678",
      "title": "Intercepting Navigation & Using Interception Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 148,
      "videoOrder": 138,
      "sourceHash": "1cd88a8cd612661138e282991a867af42943375e243baaef4ad2caec71754f08",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 4.29,
          "en": "So what's an intercepting route?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.29,
          "end": 8.49,
          "en": "Well, an intercepting route is an alternative route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.49,
          "end": 12.33,
          "en": "which sometimes gets activated depending on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.33,
          "end": 14.19,
          "en": "whether you are navigating to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.19,
          "end": 18.39,
          "en": "through an internal link from within the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.39,
          "end": 21.69,
          "en": "So if you're in that single page application mode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.69,
          "end": 24,
          "en": "and you're navigating around on the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24,
          "end": 27.09,
          "en": "or you are coming from an external link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.09,
          "end": 31.35,
          "en": "or you manually enter the URL or you reloaded the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.35,
          "end": 35.7,
          "en": "so that for the same path, different pages are shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.7,
          "end": 37.953,
          "en": "depending on how you got there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 41.85,
          "en": "That's the idea behind an intercepting route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.85,
          "end": 46.14,
          "en": "because the intercepting route essentially intercepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.14,
          "end": 49.05,
          "en": "an internal navigation request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.05,
          "end": 52.32,
          "en": "and instead of showing the page you would see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.32,
          "end": 55.86,
          "en": "if you would reload the page or come to the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.86,
          "end": 60.093,
          "en": "from outside the website, a different page will be shown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.534,
          "end": 64.773,
          "en": "And I'll show that here at the example of this image page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.76,
          "end": 68.19,
          "en": "Currently we have just one page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.19,
          "end": 72.66,
          "en": "and therefore whenever I view the details of an image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.66,
          "end": 73.95,
          "en": "I see this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.95,
          "end": 77.1,
          "en": "No matter if I got there by clicking on that image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.1,
          "end": 79.77,
          "en": "or if I got there by reloading the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.77,
          "end": 81.60300000000001,
          "en": "I always see the same page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.56,
          "end": 84.15,
          "en": "Now, if I wanted to change this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.15,
          "end": 87.18,
          "en": "I could set up such a intercepting route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.18,
          "end": 91.14,
          "en": "by creating a sibling folder to the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.14,
          "end": 94.44,
          "en": "I want to intercept though, that's not a hard requirement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.44,
          "end": 95.793,
          "en": "as you'll see in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.66,
          "end": 100.22999999999999,
          "en": "And by then, giving it a name that starts with opening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.22999999999999,
          "end": 102.53999999999999,
          "en": "and closing parentheses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.53999999999999,
          "end": 105.53999999999999,
          "en": "so not square bracket or anything like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.53999999999999,
          "end": 108.27000000000001,
          "en": "but instead regular parentheses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.27000000000001,
          "end": 112.47,
          "en": "And then after those parentheses, you repeat the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.47,
          "end": 116.4,
          "en": "of the path of the route you want to intercept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.4,
          "end": 119.37,
          "en": "So if I wanna intercept the image route here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.37,
          "end": 122.583,
          "en": "I have to add image after those parentheses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.66,
          "end": 127.17,
          "en": "And then between those parentheses, you basically have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.17,
          "end": 132.17,
          "en": "to describe the path from this folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.24,
          "end": 135.48,
          "en": "and the path segment it represents",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.48,
          "end": 138.48,
          "en": "to the segment that should be intercepted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.48,
          "end": 140.57999999999998,
          "en": "So having the same name is not enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.57999999999998,
          "end": 142.86,
          "en": "Instead, you also must describe the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.86,
          "end": 145.29,
          "en": "to get to that related folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.29,
          "end": 148.35,
          "en": "And here, if it's in the same folder, that would be achieved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.35,
          "end": 149.943,
          "en": "by adding a single dot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.35,
          "end": 153.51,
          "en": "Just as in a import path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.51,
          "end": 157.32,
          "en": "if you wanna import something from the same folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 157.32,
          "end": 159.87,
          "en": "you could do that with ./",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.87,
          "end": 163.68,
          "en": "and then the name of the file that is in the same folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.68,
          "end": 167.07,
          "en": "Now, if that intercepting route here would be set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.07,
          "end": 171.66,
          "en": "in some nested path folder, you would have to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.66,
          "end": 174.96,
          "en": "two dots here to go up one level.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.96,
          "end": 176.55,
          "en": "Just as in an import,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.55,
          "end": 179.28,
          "en": "if you need to go up one level to reach the file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.28,
          "end": 183,
          "en": "you want to import from, you have to add two dots.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183,
          "end": 185.28,
          "en": "Now, this import thing was just an example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.28,
          "end": 186.96,
          "en": "but that is how you need to configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 186.96,
          "end": 189.9,
          "en": "this intercepting route folder name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 189.9,
          "end": 193.08,
          "en": "And of course, as always, you find all the details",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 193.08,
          "end": 196.14,
          "en": "in the official documentation and there you also see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 196.14,
          "end": 199.02,
          "en": "how that would change if you would need to go up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 199.02,
          "end": 202.14,
          "en": "multiple folder segments and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 202.14,
          "end": 205.2,
          "en": "But it's pretty common that you're in the same folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 205.2,
          "end": 207.9,
          "en": "so that's probably the most important notation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 207.9,
          "end": 211.113,
          "en": "you should memorize, having this notation here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 212.16,
          "end": 215.64,
          "en": "Well, now the idea is that you add a page.js file in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 215.64,
          "end": 218.79,
          "en": "and now you define the page as it should be shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 218.79,
          "end": 221.82,
          "en": "if the navigation request was intercepted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.82,
          "end": 225.32999999999998,
          "en": "So if a user tried to visit this specific route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 225.32999999999998,
          "end": 228.48,
          "en": "whilst already being on the website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.48,
          "end": 232.92000000000002,
          "en": "And for that here, I'll actually copy and paste the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.92000000000002,
          "end": 236.01,
          "en": "from the other image page.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.01,
          "end": 239.76,
          "en": "and maybe name this intercepted image page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.76,
          "end": 244.05,
          "en": "and to see the difference here, I'll add an H2 element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.05,
          "end": 247.2,
          "en": "above that diff, where I'll say intercepted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 247.2,
          "end": 249.48,
          "en": "and wrap that all in a fragment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 249.48,
          "end": 251.37,
          "en": "And we'll make this more useful soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.37,
          "end": 254.34,
          "en": "For the moment, I'll just add this so that we can see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.34,
          "end": 256.053,
          "en": "on which page we are,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.58,
          "end": 260.97,
          "en": "because now with those changes made, if you go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.97,
          "end": 264.633,
          "en": "and you reload, you see there is no intercepted text here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 265.5,
          "end": 269.43,
          "en": "But if I go to a news and I click on the image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 269.43,
          "end": 272.82,
          "en": "this text is there, and again, if I reload, it's not there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 272.82,
          "end": 275.46,
          "en": "So we see different content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 275.46,
          "end": 279.45,
          "en": "we actually get a different page.js file being loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 279.45,
          "end": 281.73,
          "en": "depending on how we got to this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 281.73,
          "end": 286.38,
          "en": "and that's exactly the idea behind intercepting routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 286.38,
          "end": 288.78,
          "en": "Now, this can sometimes be useful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 288.78,
          "end": 292.29,
          "en": "but it's especially a useful feature when combined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 292.29,
          "end": 296.55,
          "en": "with parallel routes to, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 296.55,
          "end": 300.93,
          "en": "show the content in a modal if it's intercepted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 300.93,
          "end": 305.22,
          "en": "or as a full screen page if you came there by reloading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 305.22,
          "end": 309.753,
          "en": "or entering the link manually and that's what we'll do next.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
